- op: create  # f2c5
  at: '2026-09-28T16:30:29Z'  # f2c5
  by: agent  # f2c5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f2c5
  clock: 1  # f2c5
  nonce: f2c5  # f2c5
  data:  # f2c5
    kind: invariant  # f2c5
    title: "per-call-site collapse loses a site that carries no stamp: one in-memory bufio.NewScanner erases a real ipc_recv receive in the same function"  # f2c5
    status: violated  # f2c5
    priority: 2  # f2c5
    parent:  # f2c5
    tags:  # f2c5
    - io_boundary  # f2c5
    - taint  # f2c5
    - analysis_quality  # f2c5
    isbefore: []  # f2c5
    duplicate_of: []  # f2c5
    not_duplicate_of: []  # f2c5
    pr_ref:  # f2c5
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-28 while fixing WI-punar. Measured on the shipped io-boundaries at dev (scratchpad collapse/):\n\n  func f(r io.Reader) { sc := bufio.NewScanner(r) }                                -> ipc_recv chain bufio.NewScanner\n  func f(s string, r io.Reader) {\n      a := bufio.NewScanner(strings.NewReader(s))    // stamped io_target_kind in_memory\n      b := bufio.NewScanner(r)                        // unstamped: a parameter\n  }                                                                                -> NO ipc_recv chain (only external_potential)\n\nAdding a harmless in-memory scanner ERASED the real one's receive. Both sites collapse into one edge (deduplicate_edges). ir._absorb_per_call_site_key treats a site that OMITS the key as a disagreement and removes the singular io_target_kind, which is right. But io_target_kind_values then lists only the values sites HAVE: ['in_memory']. call_site_target_kinds returns ('in_memory',), and target_kinds_cross_no_boundary (docstring: 'EVERY collapsed call site') answers True. The unstamped site's absence is lost between the two.\n\nDIRECTION: the false-all-clear one. The call is examined (the catalogue classified it), so no chain means a must_not_exist ipc_recv claim can confirm. taint._source_call_can_mint_taint reads the same flattened tuple, so no source is minted either.\n\nSCOPE: every per_call_site key with an absence meaning (io_target_kind, io_mode, redirect_target, call_arg_shape, ...). WI-punar worked around it for JS listeners by stamping every site (#1281's second commit). Go's bufio / io.WriteString / fmt.Fprint* stamps and the WI-nunab os.File receiver stamps leave parameters unstamped, so they are exposed.\n\nFIX SHAPE (not built): make absence representable in <key>_values (e.g. a sentinel that call_site_target_kinds and call_site_modes surface as 'unknown'), so a consumer's EVERY-site rule sees the unstamped site; or have the readers treat a non-uniform _values whose members are all non-crossing as unknown. Measure the Go cohort for chains restored."  # f2c5
    fields:  # f2c5
      statement: "A collapsed edge's per-site values must let a consumer tell 'every site carries this value' from 'some sites carry it and others carry nothing': a site with no io_target_kind stamp must not be read as agreeing with a stamped sibling. VIOLATED: a stamped in_memory bufio.NewScanner beside an unstamped parameter scanner in one function reads as crossing no boundary, and the real ipc_recv chain and taint source vanish."  # f2c5
      root_cause: "ir._absorb_per_call_site_key drops the singular key when a site omits it but records only present values in <key>_values; io_boundary.call_site_target_kinds flattens that to the present values, and target_kinds_cross_no_boundary / taint._source_call_can_mint_taint then see only the stamped sites."  # f2c5
