- op: discuss  # eed6
  at: '2026-09-28T20:12:01Z'  # eed6
  by: agent  # eed6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # eed6
  clock: 4  # eed6
  nonce: eed6  # eed6
  message: "Fixed in PR #1283 (4a90935b2b + manifest dbfeca8c7e). Root cause as filed: ir._absorb_per_call_site_key dropped the singular key when a site omitted it but listed only present values in <key>_values. The collapse now lists an unstamped site as None (JSON null), sorted first so the cap never drops it, and merges an absorbed edge's own _values (apply_external_id_remap can absorb an already-collapsed edge; its values were lost before). Readers: io_boundary.call_site_modes / call_site_target_kinds return None for that site and read a malformed member as None instead of dropping it. Consumers give None the single-unstamped-call meaning: _boundary_for_target_kind -> (False, None) so target_kinds_cross_no_boundary is False, resolve_target_kind_across_sites abstains and taint._source_call_can_mint_taint mints; the mode seam reads None as the default read (resolve_mode_boundary), so mode_spanned_boundaries reports both fs boundaries; taint._name_flow_indexes: a None env_var site empties the source name set, a None redirect_origin_names site makes the sink set None (the INV-fumod pair proof abstains).\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE on merged dev dbfeca8c7e (shipped CLI):\n- the filed Go repro (in-memory bufio.NewScanner + parameter scanner): io-boundaries -> ipc_recv bufio.NewScanner, fs_read bufio.Scanner.Scan (dev before: neither).\n- same + exec.Command(b.Text()), untrusted_input -> subprocess: violated, 2 flows, rc 1 (before: inconclusive, 0 flows, rc 2).\n- SIBLING found while fixing, the mode seam: json.load(open(p)) + open(q,'w'), must_not_exist fs_read: violated rc 1 (before: CONFIRMED rc 0, a false all-clear).\nTests: core test_per_site_absence_is_a_value.py; lang-mainstream test_collapsed_site_keeps_its_crossing.py (the three repros, each with a one-site control).\n\nSCOPE, enumerated by grep over packages/*/src: the only readers of any <key>_values are call_site_modes, call_site_target_kinds, and taint's env_var_values / redirect_origin_names_values reads, and all four are fixed. call_arg_shape_values and redirect_target(_resolved)_values have no reader; their consumers read the singular key only, which is absent whenever sites disagree (unchanged, conservative). Cached behaviour maps are keyed on an analyzer-identity hash of the source, so a pre-fix map is not reused.\n\nA/B (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/rajak_09282026/RESULT.md), 7 repos (coredns, alertmanager, fastapi, prometheus, podman, beads, feast): ZERO chains gained or lost, 28/28 verdicts identical. The null-bearing io edges on that cohort are 7 os.File.Close [None, host_path] (Close is not target-kind-decided) and 2 open sites (feast's already spanned r/w; podman's is a project method). Correct on the constructed instances; NO measured corpus effect -- not a recall gain. The WI-punar every-site stamping in js_ts is no longer needed for correctness; it stays because the crossing stamp names the target kind (comment updated)."  # eed6
